Structure integration
Original local code in crates/isr-core/src/geometry.rs and
crates/isr-core/src/counters.rs exports line-break and transformed bounds,
measures closed-details descendants at their open-layout positions, and materializes static
counter-generated text for shaping in a second style/layout pass. The structure, geometry, effects and counter integration remains local integration code.
The vendored Blitz modifications cover SVG opt-in, text/control shaping,
@font-face descriptors, synthetic font painting and automatic table sizing.
The checked-in patch files capture these differences from the pinned source.
The four probes reuse the unchanged public font already identified above.

Known upstream parse-order limitation: if a host process constructs a Blitz
DocumentConfig::default() before its first call to the renderer, Blitz may cache
the default user-agent stylesheet before the counter preference is enabled,
permanently omitting its counter rules for that process. The renderer initializes
this preference before building its own configs; an upstream fix is needed for
host-created early configurations.

All fixture markup, CSS, SVG paths, comparison tools and gate code are original work for
html-native-renderer under Apache-2.0, apart from the embedded font noted above.

